+    * The original game is never written; the result is a new folder.
+    * A file extension never changes (scripts refer to files by name).
+    * A file is replaced only when the new version is smaller (or, in the
+      old-PC video mode, when it is easier to play) and lasts the same.
+    * Any error on one file leaves that file as it was.
+
+ffmpeg
+    Audio and video need ``ffmpeg``, a separate program that is run, never
+    imported. It is looked up next to LinguaNova (folder build), in the user's
+    tools folder (downloaded on first use by the portable build), at a path
+    the user chose, and finally on PATH. Without it only images are processed.
